    "collapsible_content_jF6Q7J": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_D7di3E": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How does the Phoenix Gravity Filter compare to plastic jugs or other filters?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The Phoenix Gravity is one of the most advanced filtration systems on the market. With a Phoenix Gravity System, your water is purified through three-stages of activated carbon filtration to remove 99.9% of contaminants including bacteria, parasites, cysts, pesticides, heavy metals and more. Our highly dense filtration system uses the highest quality coconut shells (CTC 60) to create a tortuous path that traps physical contaminants that are more than 20 times smaller than jug filters.</p><p>Our stainless steel chambers not only prevent microplastics and other harmful chemicals from leaching into your water, but also hold significantly more purified water than the average jug. This makes it even easier for you to enjoy fresh, nutrient-rich hydration - whenever you need it most. Unlike Reverse Osmosis (RO) filters, the gravity system does not require electricity to run or a plumber to install - and it won’t strip your water of the healthy nutrients your body benefits from.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_W4xnAC": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I set it up myself?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Absolutely. The Phoenix Gravity Mini is designed for easy DIY set-up within minutes - no plumber, electricity or prior knowledge required. We’ll send detailed instructions, along with instructions on how to prime your cartridge, with your Phoenix Gravity Mini.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_tWhmT6": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I clean my carbon cartridges?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, it’s simple! You can easily clean your filter in your home using tap water and a soft brush or mild abrasive. We’ll include detailed instructions when we send your Phoenix Gravity Filter.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_H8Qyp3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How does the Phoenix Gravity Filter compare to plastic jugs or other filters?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The Phoenix Gravity is one of the most advanced filtration systems on the market. With a Phoenix Gravity System, your water is purified through two-stages of activated carbon filtration to remove 99.9% of contaminants including bacteria, parasites, cysts, pesticides, heavy metals and more.  This means we can trap physical contaminants that are more than 20 times smaller than jug filters. Combined with our higher filtration contact time we are 20 times more powerful than typical jug filters and those using granular carbon.</p><p>Our stainless steel chambers not only prevent microplastics and other harmful chemicals from leaching into your water, but also hold significantly more purified water than the average jug. This makes it even easier for you to enjoy fresh, nutrient-rich hydration - whenever you need it most. Unlike Reverse Osmosis (RO) filters, the gravity system does not require electricity to run or a plumber to install - and it won’t strip your water of the healthy nutrients your body benefits from.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_UHMcUe": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are Phoenix Gravity Smart Carbon Cartridges compatible with my gravity-fed system?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes! Phoenix Gravity Smart Carbon Cartridges are precision-engineered to work with nearly all gravity-fed water systems. They’re built for reliable performance and deliver clean, safe, great-tasting water every time.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
